CONTEXT Twins IN ENGLISH
PURPOSE CONTEXT Twins
{+ The same file is included twice, under two aliases.
Each alias stands for a copy of its own, so `North.name` and `South.name` are two relations
and `North.Person` and `South.Person` are two concepts. +}

INCLUDE "../contexts/registry.adl" AS North
INCLUDE "../contexts/registry.adl" AS South

RELATION moved[North.Person*South.Person] [UNI,INJ]
POPULATION moved[North.Person*South.Person] CONTAINS [ ("p1", "p1") ]

-- A pair that exists in one copy only, to show that the populations are separate.
POPULATION South.name[South.Person*South.Name] CONTAINS [ ("p3", "Carla") ]

RULE sameName : moved |- North.name;V[North.Name*South.Name];South.name~
ROLE Clerk MAINTAINS sameName

ENDCONTEXT
